{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-platforms-online-payments-split-transactions-split-payments-at-authorization","reason":"Full independent review of all 2,444 pinned raw lines matched the trusted SHA-256, five exact quotes and locators, and accepted receipt against candidate and suggestions. Prerequisites, valid-capability and closed/nonexistent-destination fallbacks, conditional split fields, no-store payment-facilitator data, capture override, and the table-versus-example store placement conflict are otherwise represented accurately. One material webhook-example conflict is unqualified: the prose and transfer payload show commission incoming to the liable balance account, but the commission transaction.created sample at raw lines 2354-2393 shows amount -500 and the user's balance account; the fee transfer sample uses a second user balance account at lines 1939-1942 while its transaction.created sample at 2022-2061 names the first. The draft's statement that these example credits and deductions map cleanly to their respective user/liable accounts can mislead reconciliation or webhook implementation."}
