{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-platforms-online-payments-checkout-components","reason":"Independently read all 1,131 pinned raw lines, verified SHA-256 and all five exact quotes at their cited lines, and matched accepted candidate/suggestions and fixed Q1/Q2. The draft correctly captures the server-created Sessions and client Web Components route, credential/role and UI constraints, redirect handling, fixed session-result status, asynchronous AUTHORISATION outcome, and test-to-live boundaries. One material scope boundary is absent: the captured guide contains no split-instruction field or booking procedure, yet it is a Platforms checkout source. A reader asking whether following this Components /sessions flow allocates a shopper payment to a platform user's balance account could be led to treat checkout/authorization completion as split booking. The existing Platforms online-payments source is the separate route for that question; a direct qualification here is needed before promotion."}
{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-platforms-in-person-payments-split-transactions-split-payments-at-capture","reason":"Full independent review of the 1,663-line pinned raw matched the trusted SHA-256, accepted candidate/suggestions equality and all five exact quote locators. The draft correctly covers delayed/separate-capture prerequisites, payment-request override, changed-amount liable fallback, unsupported capture-time Tip/Surcharge, conditional split fields, format-only validation, CAPTURE versus received response, and its identified currency and fee-target inconsistencies. One additional material conflict in the illustrative webhook sequence remains undisclosed: commission prose and transfer payloads describe an incoming liable-account credit, but the commission transaction.created sample at lines 1599-1627 shows amount -400 and a user's balance account; the commission captured transfer itself changes liable-account ID at lines 1498-1501. The fee transfer names the second user balance account at lines 1019-1022 and 1174-1176, while fee transaction.created names the first at lines 1291-1295. Readers could otherwise treat the example booked sign/account as authoritative despite the otherwise sound stage distinction."}
