{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-platforms-online-payments-transaction-fees","reason":"Independently read the full 1,458-line pinned raw and matched SHA-256 9c4ccd0694ebdca3b5e573bada4d2b5c57565863f34523a0e5578115158b4f20. All five quoted strings match their cited lines; the accepted receipt, candidate and suggestions agree. The source accurately preserves online/POS scope, fee taxonomy and aggregate precedence, excluded unallocable costs, liable-account default, payment-versus-booking boundary and the EUR/USD and AdyenFees prose conflicts. The reciprocal suggestion targets the existing adyen-platforms ## Sources anchor. One material warning remains incomplete: the worked fee webhook examples themselves cannot be treated as a consistent per-split reconciliation trail. The AcquiringFees captured transfer unexpectedly names BA...02 rather than user BA...01 (raw 1008-1011 versus 855-857 and 1127-1129); the AdyenFees booked transaction names user BA...01 despite its liable-account transfer (1436-1439 versus 1163-1166 and 1317-1320); the AdyenFees booked transfer ID differs from the preceding AdyenFees transfer (1416-1417 versus 1385-1387); and both fee-type booked examples reuse the same transaction ID (1100-1103 and 1409-1413). This matters because the candidate tells readers to match those records at the correct grain while identifying only the line-1141 prose error."}
{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-platforms-in-person-payments-split-transactions-split-refunds-refund-split-instructions","reason":"The full 1282-line pinned raw was independently read in complete chunks and matches SHA-256 ae8bee550263717fe055f3587da84ec5b759ae97845de4a0c5ef83c0f9876edb; all five receipt quotes match their exact raw lines. The candidate and fixed Q1/Q2 correctly preserve referenced Terminal reversal scope, standalone and payment-method limits, original split references and credited-account restriction, partial major-unit amount/currency fields, full-refund omissions, and Success/REFUND REQUESTED versus asynchronous CANCEL_OR_REFUND outcome. A material tracking qualification remains: raw line 325 explicitly says the balance-platform webhook examples are based on an online refund request, while the candidate presents their stages in this Terminal procedure without that source boundary. Also, raw line 207 labels POIData.POITransactionID.TransactionID the refund PSP reference, but the response example has TF995R5G6L2GWR82 there and a different AdditionalResponse.pspReference KHLWK3Z3FZTQ7RT5 at line 237; the separate online-derived webhook examples use modificationPspReference QFQTPCQ8HXSKGK82. The statement that the response provides a refund PSP reference and the generic original/modification correlation language could imply these example IDs map to one Terminal reversal, which this page does not establish. The other tracking/example inconsistencies are already flagged. The reciprocal source link is accurate and fits the existing adyen-platforms Sources anchor."}
