{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-platforms-in-person-payments-split-transactions-split-refunds-refund-original-split","reason":"Full independent review of all 1,079 pinned raw lines matched the trusted SHA-256, accepted candidate/suggestions equality and five exact quotes. The source correctly distinguishes an inherited original-payment split in a full referenced Terminal API reversal from unproven partial-refund math or capture-override inheritance, and preserves TransactionID/TimeStamp, Success-as-receipt, asynchronous CANCEL_OR_REFUND, original versus refund PSP references, and USD 188 versus later sample amount conflicts. One material ledger-example conflict remains insufficiently qualified: the commission transfer prose and payloads debit the liable balance account, but commission transaction.created at lines 751-759 names the user's account; the initial commission received event also has a -7500 mutation despite its USD 10 amount at lines 494-528. The fee transfer payloads name a second user balance account at lines 803-806 and 953-956, while fee transaction.created names the first at lines 1063-1066. The draft's balance-movement statement could be read as a reliable booked-account map although these examples disagree."}
