{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-platforms-multi-pay-in","reason":"Independently read the full 126-line pinned raw and matched SHA-256 369d2dc3e22ea07822b8c2e6010f1fdde7d00ed6c7052feb2318126860f37efc. All five quotes match their cited lines; accepted receipt, candidate and suggestions agree. The source and fixed Q1/Q2 accurately preserve online-only integration, Checkout/Transfers credentials, webhook and account-holder capability gates, no separate authorization/capture, Adyen-held multi pay-in account per partner, 24-hour allocation, liable-account fallback, illustrative flow and EUR/USD refund-diagram conflict. A focused concept fills a genuine gap and the Platforms reciprocal route is apt. One refund claim overstates the pinned evidence: the source says the pay-in partner transfers the refund amount to the user's customer (raw line 85), but does not specify the customer's payment method as destination. The existing detailed refund source also preserves the partner-versus-Adyen boundary without asserting that method. This matters for a query about who sends the refund and how it reaches the customer."}
